---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { site, doc } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'November 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support · Siple"
  description="How to get help with Siple: report a bug, ask a question, and answers to common questions about editions, settings and links."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" class="sup">
    <article class="wrap sup__in">
      <header class="sup__head">
        <h1 class="display--md">Support</h1>
        <p class="lede">Where to get help with Siple, and answers to a few common questions.</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Get help</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Bugs and feature requests:</strong> open an issue on <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>GitHub</a>. Say which edition you run (direct download, Mac App Store, Microsoft Store or Flatpak), your operating system and the Siple version.</li>
          <li><strong>Anything else:</strong> email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact}`}>{site.contact}</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Read first:</strong> the <a href={site.docs}>user guide</a>, its <a href={doc.faq}>questions and answers</a> and <a href={doc.troubleshooting}>troubleshooting</a> pages.</li>
          <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> the <a href={site.privacy}>privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Logs can contain phone numbers and SIP messages. Look them over before you attach them to a public issue. The troubleshooting guide shows <a href={doc.logs}>how to collect and share them safely</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Common questions</h2>

        <h3>Where does Siple keep my settings?</h3>
        <p>In a folder that depends on how you installed it. The file is <code>config.toml</code>; logs and the rest sit next to it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>macOS, direct download: <code>~/Library/Application Support/Siple/</code></li>
          <li>Windows, direct download: <code>%APPDATA%\Siple\</code></li>
          <li>Linux, tarball and AppImage: <code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/siple/</code> (usually <code>~/.config/siple/</code>)</li>
          <li>Mac App Store: <code>~/Library/Group Containers/VUDU4KEQ99.io.zyno.siple/Siple/</code></li>
          <li>Microsoft Store: <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages\&lt;package family name&gt;\LocalState\Siple\</code></li>
          <li>Flatpak: <code>~/.var/app/io.zyno.siple/config/siple/</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Settings &gt; Advanced has an <strong>Open config</strong> button. Details are in the <a href={doc.configLocation}>configuration reference</a>.</p>

        <h3>Phone links don't open in Siple.</h3>
        <p>In the direct downloads, check that <strong>Open sip:, sips:, tel:, callto: and siple: setup links</strong> is on in Settings, then make Siple the default app for those links in your operating system. <a href={doc.links}>The links guide</a> has the steps. In the Mac App Store and Microsoft Store editions there is no such setting: the app declares the links when it is installed. If another app still opens them, choose Siple as the default app for that link type in the system settings.</p>

        <h3>Does uninstalling the Microsoft Store version delete my settings?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Windows removes the app's data folder with the app, so your configuration, accounts and logs go too. Copy <code>config.toml</code> out of the folder above first if you want to keep it. Updates keep your data.</p>

        <h3>I use the direct download and want the Mac App Store version.</h3>
        <p>Quit the direct build before you install the App Store version. Both use the same app identifier, so macOS can confuse them while both are installed. The App Store edition keeps its own settings and starts with none, so add your accounts again, or copy the file from the direct build's folder.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sup__in {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-top: 96px;
    padding-bottom: 120px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .sup__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .sup h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .sup p,
  .sup li {
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .sup p + p {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .sup ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sup h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
  }
  .sup code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .sup__in {
      padding-top: 56px;
      padding-bottom: 80px;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
